{"event":"run","task":"L2","executor":"haiku","plan":"sonnet","arm":"FULL","rep":1,"modelId":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","pinnedSha":"c62bcf6420c24c7e43c078d72aade6afcf25a765","costUsd":1.6023407999999997,"invocations":[{"role":"primary","cost":1.0880697999999998,"turns":102,"wallS":495,"timedOut":false},{"role":"contract-salvage","cost":0.025231599999999996},{"role":"reviewer","cost":0.1698428,"wallS":146},{"role":"reviewer-salvage","cost":0.0111328},{"role":"revision","cost":0.3080638,"turns":9,"wallS":135}],"contract":{"summary":"Pluggable queue backend refactoring complete. Created QueueBackend interface with SqsQueueBackend and InMemoryQueueBackend implementations. Updated enqueueWorkItems() to accept QueueBackend instead of SQSClient. Added RetryableError handling for failedIds. Updated 14 lambda handlers mechanically. All 737 tests pass.","filesChanged":["packages/core/src/queue/backends.ts","packages/core/src/queue/index.ts","packages/core/__tests__/queue.test.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/trigger-task.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/enrich-issue.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/revise-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/quick-task.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/merge-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/reconcile-enqueuer.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/plan-tasks.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/bootstrap-repo.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/review-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/rebase-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/webhook-handler.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/generate-architecture.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/reconcile.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/bootstrap-project.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/create-issues.ts"],"testsGreen":true},"rawReview":"Based on my review, I've identified a critical correctness issue:\n\n**Issue: SqsQueueBackend doesn't extract failed message IDs from the SQS response**\n\nLooking at packages/core/src/queue/backends.ts lines 12-31, the `SqsQueueBackend.sendBatch()` method:\n\n```typescript\nasync sendBatch(...): Promise<{ failedIds: string[] }> {\n  // ... setup code ...\n  await this.client.send(command);\n  return { failedIds: [] };  // ← ALWAYS returns empty, never checks response\n}\n```\n\nAccording to AWS SDK v3, `SendMessageBatchCommandOutput` includes a `Failed?: BatchResultErrorEntry[]` array. When SQS batch operations partially fail (which is normal), they return failure details in this array. The implementation should extract these:\n\n```typescript\nconst response = await this.client.send(command);\nconst failedIds = (response.Failed || []).map(f => f.Id);\nreturn { failedIds };\n```\n\n**Why this matters:** When real SQS failures occur (permissions, malformed messages, etc.), the system will silently ignore them instead of retrying. The failedIds path in `enqueueWorkItems` will never be triggered for actual SQS failures.\n\n**Why tests pass:** The test mock returns `{}` by default, so `response.Failed` is undefined, masking the bug.\n\nAll other aspects are correct:\n- ✓ Interface and implementations defined properly\n- ✓ Batching and grouping logic preserved\n- ✓ All callers updated consistently  \n- ✓ Test coverage for InMemoryQueueBackend and failedIds path\n- ✓ RetryableError thrown correctly when failures are reported\n\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"REQUEST_CHANGES\", \"issues\": [\"SqsQueueBackend.sendBatch() doesn't extract failed message IDs from AWS response - it always returns failedIds: [], preventing retry of actual SQS failures\"]}\n```","reviewVerdict":"REQUEST_CHANGES","reviewIssues":["SqsQueueBackend.sendBatch() doesn't extract failed message IDs from AWS response - it always returns failedIds: [], preventing retry of actual SQS failures"],"revised":true,"buildGreen":true,"visibleGreen":true,"holdoutPass":true,"holdoutTail":[" Test Files  1 passed (1)","      Tests  3 passed (3)"],"testEdits":["packages/core/__tests__/queue.test.ts"],"success":true,"silentFailure":false,"blocks":0,"changedFiles":["packages/core/__tests__/queue.test.ts","packages/core/src/queue/index.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/bootstrap-project.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/bootstrap-repo.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/create-issues.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/enrich-issue.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/generate-architecture.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/merge-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/plan-tasks.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/quick-task.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/rebase-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/reconcile-enqueuer.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/reconcile.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/review-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/revise-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/trigger-task.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/webhook-handler.ts"],"diffstat":"17 files changed, 137 insertions(+), 49 deletions(-)","wallSecTotal":871,"globalCostAfter":50.9745}
{"event":"run","task":"L2","executor":"haiku","plan":"sonnet","arm":"FULL","rep":2,"modelId":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","pinnedSha":"c62bcf6420c24c7e43c078d72aade6afcf25a765","costUsd":1.7131967000000001,"invocations":[{"role":"primary","cost":1.1736397,"turns":120,"wallS":496,"timedOut":false},{"role":"contract-salvage","cost":0.0264546},{"role":"reviewer","cost":0.22669130000000004,"wallS":172},{"role":"reviewer-salvage","cost":0.0120695},{"role":"revision","cost":0.2743416,"turns":7,"wallS":78}],"contract":{"summary":"Implemented pluggable queue backend with SqsQueueBackend preserving existing behavior and InMemoryQueueBackend for testing. Updated enqueueWorkItems to accept QueueBackend interface and throw RetryableError on failed IDs. Mechanically updated all 14 handlers to create module-level SqsQueueBackend instances.","filesChanged":["packages/core/src/queue/backends.ts","packages/core/src/queue/index.ts","packages/core/__tests__/queue.test.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/trigger-task.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/enrich-issue.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/revise-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/quick-task.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/merge-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/reconcile-enqueuer.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/plan-tasks.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/bootstrap-repo.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/review-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/rebase-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/webhook-handler.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/generate-architecture.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/reconcile.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/bootstrap-project.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/create-issues.ts","packages/lambdas/__tests__/integration/helpers.ts"],"testsGreen":true},"rawReview":"Based on my adversarial review, I've identified the following:\n\n## Findings:\n\n**CRITICAL ISSUE:** \n\n**SqsQueueBackend ignores SQS batch send failures** (line 28 in backends.ts) - `SendMessageBatchCommand` returns a response that may contain a `Failed` array with entries that failed to send, but the implementation always returns `{ failedIds: [] }` without checking the response. This means actual SQS failures would be silently ignored, defeating the failedIds error-handling contract defined in the interface.\n\nThe task specifies: \"If a sendBatch result reports failedIds, throw a RetryableError\". However, SqsQueueBackend never reports any failedIds because it doesn't inspect the SQS response. The failure-handling path is only testable via `InMemoryQueueBackend` and mocks, not with real SQS usage.\n\n**SECONDARY ISSUE:**\n\n**Integration test mock signature mismatch** (packages/lambdas/__tests__/integration/helpers.ts, line ~285) - The `enqueueWorkItems` mock declares only the `items` parameter but the function now takes two parameters `(items, backend)`. The mock should include:\n\n```typescript\nenqueueWorkItems: vi.fn(async (items: Array<Record<string, unknown>>, backend: any) => {\n```\n\nThis creates a type inconsistency even though JavaScript ignores the extra parameter.\n\n**Positive:** All other aspects are correctly implemented - interface definition, InMemoryQueueBackend, refactored enqueueWorkItems with proper batching, and all 17 lambda handlers updated consistently. Tests pass (42 queue tests).\n\n<answer>{\"verdict\": \"REQUEST_CHANGES\", \"issues\": [\"SqsQueueBackend.sendBatch() does not check the SQS response for Failed entries; it always returns empty failedIds array, meaning actual SQS batch failures are silently ignored instead of being reported and retried\", \"Integration test mock for enqueueWorkItems has incorrect signature—should declare backend parameter: vi.fn(async (items, backend) => ...)\"]}</answer>","reviewVerdict":"REQUEST_CHANGES","reviewIssues":["SqsQueueBackend.sendBatch() does not check the SQS response for Failed entries; it always returns empty failedIds array, meaning actual SQS batch failures are silently ignored instead of being reported and retried","Integration test mock for enqueueWorkItems has incorrect signature—should declare backend parameter: vi.fn(async (items, backend) => ...)"],"revised":true,"buildGreen":true,"visibleGreen":true,"holdoutPass":true,"holdoutTail":[" Test Files  1 passed (1)","      Tests  3 passed (3)"],"testEdits":["packages/core/__tests__/queue.test.ts","packages/lambdas/__tests__/integration/helpers.ts"],"success":true,"silentFailure":false,"blocks":0,"changedFiles":["packages/core/__tests__/queue.test.ts","packages/core/src/queue/index.ts","packages/lambdas/__tests__/integration/helpers.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/bootstrap-project.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/bootstrap-repo.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/create-issues.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/enrich-issue.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/generate-architecture.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/merge-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/plan-tasks.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/quick-task.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/rebase-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/reconcile-enqueuer.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/reconcile.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/review-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/revise-pr.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/trigger-task.ts","packages/lambdas/src/handlers/webhook-handler.ts"],"diffstat":"18 files changed, 122 insertions(+), 50 deletions(-)","wallSecTotal":840,"globalCostAfter":52.6877}
